A||||4||Scott||Grand Am front brakes||||1||
Z||000000||Scott||05-24-2001||11:36 PM||||I've been away from Fieros for a while, and lately I've heard of using Grand Am brakes on Fieros.  Does entail using the Grand Am rotors and calipers with factory Fiero hubs, or is there more involved (adapters, custom hubs, & etc.)?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Devotshka||05-24-2001||11:40 PM||||For the rear of the Fiero, it is a direct bolt-in replacement; rotors, calipers, pads get replaced.  However you will no longer have a parking brake (due to these being FRONT brakes from a grand am).<BR>For the front end, you need to have your old rotors machined down to hubs, have longer studs installed, then the g/a rotors will slide over those 'new' hubs.  I believe there are a few minor modifications that need to be made for caliper mounting (little bit of grinding).<BR>I'm sure someone else can add more info to this, the fronts are kinda foggy for me, haven't thought about it in a while. The rears however, were a cinch.||||reg||1
Z||000002||PBJ||05-24-2001||11:42 PM||||Here is how I found about it and also performed the job with great results.<P>went to <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroproject.com</A>  then went to "links" to "fiero secrects" and go down to brakes.  Beretta and Grand am are the same.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GTPete.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fierowrecker||05-24-2001||11:45 PM||||Hey Scott!<BR>There are a number of sites that cover the subject very well...<BR>Basicly, you can use the 89 Grand Am front calipers and rotors on the rear of the Fiero with no modifications...<BR>There is a bit of grinding on the front knuckle, as well as machine work to the rotor/hub to use the Grand Am rotors on the front...<BR>I am running the Fiero calipers on the front, and the Grand Am conversion on the rear of my 86 2M4, and I am using the stock master cylinder...<BR>There are many pro and con issues with this change, but I like it!!!<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000004||Rob Durham||05-24-2001||11:52 PM||||I just did the front and rear brakes on my 87 GT using the info from  <A HREF="http://fierozone.tripod.com/realbrakes/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://fierozone.tripod.com/realbrakes/index.html</A>  it was very easy and there is an unbelievable differance in the braking power.<P>Rob||||reg||10
